    "result_text": "That's just JaCoCo coverage excludes for generated code \u2014 not test exclusions. The implementation is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for owners. When a request includes an ISO `birthDate`, the API now returns `ageBand` (`MINOR` / `ADULT` / `SENIOR`) computed against the owner's `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges made, following the repo's existing pattern for derived owner fields (`membershipLevel`, `contactPreference`, etc.):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `birthDate` (date) input to the `OwnerFields` schema, and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` schema. These drive the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` and are auto-mapped by MapStruct by name.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` field (with getter/setter mapped to a `birth_date` column) and a `@Transient getAgeBand()` that returns `MINOR` (< 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+) using `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate)`, or `null` when either date is absent.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in the hsqldb, h2, mysql, and postgres `schema.sql` files.\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 the seed inserts are positional, so I appended a `NULL` for the new column to each owners row (the other DBs use named-column inserts and needed no change).\n\nThe full test suite passes:\n\n```\nTests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```\n\nThe one acceptance test (`coreDerivesAgeBand`) creates an owner with `birthDate` `1990-01-01` and asserts `ageBand` = `ADULT` on read \u2014 confirmed green.",
